/**
  @page examples-mmg-casting Using an MMG mesh in Rodin
  @brief Share the geometry interface and manage remeshing lifetimes.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section examples-mmg-cast-intro Mesh interfaces

  `MMG::Mesh` derives from `Geometry::Mesh<Context::Local>`. It can therefore
  be supplied to local finite element spaces and variational problems through
  the geometry interface. Its additional metadata records MMG corners, ridges
  and required entities.

  @section examples-mmg-cast-create Initialize from generated geometry

  Assignment from a plain geometry mesh copies its topology and coordinates
  and clears MMG-specific metadata. Apply feature labels after that assignment:

  @snippet MMG/MeshIO.cpp mmg-io-create

  @section examples-mmg-cast-fes Scope spaces around remeshing

  A finite element space borrows its mesh and determines degrees of freedom
  from the current topology. The adaptation example constructs a nodal size
  field on that mesh and passes it to MMG:

  @snippet MMG/MeshAdaptation.cpp mmg-adapt-call

  After the call, the old size field's topology-dependent representation is
  no longer used. The program leaves its scope before continuing. Construct
  fresh spaces, trial/test functions and problems for the new mesh; transfer
  fields through a specified interpolation or projection procedure when their
  state is needed for the next solve.

  @section examples-mmg-cast-io Keep the feature representation

  @ref examples-mmg-simple_io "MEDIT I/O" stores the MMG metadata used by the
  wrapper. Passing the object through a plain geometry interface provides the
  operations supported by that interface. Select an MMG-aware representation
  when the corner, ridge and required-entity sets must be retained.

  @section examples-mmg-cast-see-also Continue

  - @ref examples-mmg-simple_io "Checked metadata round trip"
  - @ref examples-mmg-mesh_adaptation "Adapt to a nodal size field"
  - @ref guides-numerical-contracts "Mesh and field lifetimes"
*/
